WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.633
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.750
- Hey guys, I'm Kelly.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.640
And today, Jasmine has challenged me

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.600
to make all of my meals for the day

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.900
in a mug in the microwave.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.660
In the restaurant world, we
call this bad boy Chef Mike

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.130
and he's definitely not
getting any Michelin stars,

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.580
so I'm a little iffy about it.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.290
And at the end, Jasmine is
going to give me a yay or a nay.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.160
Let's see if we can whip
up some gourmet meals

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.084
that Jasmine likes.

00:00:26.084 --> 00:00:28.270
All right, first up is breakfast.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.120
I don't know about you,

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.690
but I definitely didn't eat
anything this fancy in college.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:34.540
It was a bagel, maybe toast.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.950
But today, I am making a
ricotta blueberry mug cake.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.273
It's basically like a
fancy pancake in a bowl.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:44.660
So we have some ricotta,
some maple syrup, butter,

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.770
because it makes everything better.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:47.710
- [Jasmine] Yeah, it does.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.550
- Milk, I'm actually using oat milk today,

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.460
because I'm making it for Jasmine,

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.181
and I know she loves oat milk.

00:00:53.181 --> 00:00:55.331
- [Jasmine] Awww.
- Just gonna whisk that.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.100
So this is a little
challenging trying to whisk

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.530
and make sure it's all combined
in this tiny little mug.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:04.710
This is a no-no in culinary world.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.390
You need to have a bigger
bowl, so you can get in there.

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:08.780
- [Jasmine] I actually
have a hack for this.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.613
- What?
- [Jasmine] I do this

00:01:09.613 --> 00:01:11.244
and I just go.
- Oh.

00:01:11.244 --> 00:01:14.347
Jasmine is telling me to go
like this and she's right.

00:01:14.347 --> 00:01:16.130
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.374
This is perfect, okay.

00:01:17.374 --> 00:01:18.810
Now we're gonna add our dry.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:23.660
We just have some flour,
baking powder, and salt.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.493
Always add salt.

00:01:24.493 --> 00:01:25.970
I feel like I say that in every video,

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:28.837
but I love salt and it
makes you feel good.

00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:32.200
So this is like an upgraded
fancy pancake for Jasmine,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.480
because I've added ricotta,
which is gonna give it like

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:37.460
a little bit of a tang and
also make it super tender.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.921
Now I'm gonna fold in some
blueberries and that's it.

00:01:40.921 --> 00:01:41.920
(spatula banging)

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.050
You're definitely gonna wanna cover

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:44.360
all of the meals we're making today,

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.140
so it doesn't explode in your microwave

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.520
and make a huge mess.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.020
If you're not comfortable with saran wrap,

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.470
just put a plate on top,
just cover it, trust me.

00:01:52.974 --> 00:01:54.200
(microwave beeping)

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:55.657
All right, so I'm gonna
cook it for three minutes,

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.660
check it, and then if it needs more time,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:58.824
I'll just add one more minute.

00:01:58.824 --> 00:01:59.740
(microwave beeping)

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:01.980
So just a heads up, your
cook time will differ

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.280
depending on how powerful
your microwave is,

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:05.982
so just keep checking
in to see where it's at.

00:02:05.982 --> 00:02:08.982
(microwave beeping)

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.240
To make my streusel topping,

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.642
I'm gonna add some flour, brown sugar.

00:02:13.642 --> 00:02:16.050
Just toss that together.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:20.000
A little pinch of cinnamon
and then some cubed butter.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:20.890
Make sure it's cold.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:23.410
Because I'm really trying
to impress Jasmine,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.560
so I am making a brown sugar crumble.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.340
Everything should be evenly combined

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.940
and looks like one cohesive
mass instead of like

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.540
bits of flour, bits of butter.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.610
So I'm just gonna put some on top.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:35.517
I'm gonna cover it one more time.

00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:36.670
Put this back in the microwave

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:38.967
for another minute and a half.

00:02:38.967 --> 00:02:40.440
All right, let's see
if Chef Mike failed me,

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.520
or, oh, oh.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.360
I don't think I should have put

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.030
the saran wrap on the second time,

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.860
'cause it's like trapping moisture in

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:49.621
and it's just, it's not a crumble.

00:02:49.621 --> 00:02:51.471
Chef Mike has failed me,

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:53.280
but I'm gonna put it back in the microwave

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.850
and see if I can get those
bits a little crunchier.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.540
All right, I just checked on
it, it's definitely working,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.134
but I'm gonna give it 30 more seconds.

00:02:59.134 --> 00:03:00.670
(microwave beeping)

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:01.540
All right.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.494
Honestly, it doesn't look that great,

00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:05.930
but I can smell it and I
think it's gonna taste great.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.090
All right, so to garnish this,

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.520
I'm just gonna add some fresh blueberries.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.240
I know Jasmine hates warm fruit,

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.170
so I'm hoping these cold blueberries

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.887
will help balance out
everything and she'll love it.

00:03:14.887 --> 00:03:16.350
And to finish, I'm just gonna garnish

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:17.993
with a little powdered sugar.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.680
I'm still not satisfied with the look.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:22.860
So I went and grabbed a little mint.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.693
It's so cute.

00:03:23.693 --> 00:03:25.490
Just adds a pop of color.

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.720
All right, let's bring Jasmine in

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.270
and see if she gives this
ricotta blueberry cake

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.760
a yay or a nay.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.593
All right, you ready to try it?

00:03:31.593 --> 00:03:32.790
- [Jasmine] Yes.
- All right, here you go.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.043
- Thank you!

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:36.720
I love.
(hands clapping)

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:37.553
- Yay!

00:03:37.553 --> 00:03:39.790
- Whenever I think mug meal,
I think mac and cheese,

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.500
lasagna, pizza in a mug.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.295
No one ever thinks of
blueberry ricotta mug cake.

00:03:44.295 --> 00:03:45.810
- What do you think of the ricotta?

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.070
- So creamy.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.205
- And you get that little bit of tang?

00:03:48.205 --> 00:03:49.038
- Mhm.

00:03:49.038 --> 00:03:50.143
This is a Jasmine yay.

00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:51.410
I know lunch is coming up soon.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.580
- All right, all right,
time to get to work.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.413
Get out of here, let's go!

00:03:53.413 --> 00:03:54.682
- All right, I'm taking
this though. (laughs)

00:03:54.682 --> 00:03:56.894
- Next up for lunch, I'm making Jasmine

00:03:56.894 --> 00:03:58.632
a Thai curry noodle soup.

00:03:58.632 --> 00:04:00.690
It is not the most authentic,

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:01.640
but I think it will give you

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.200
that curry fix you're looking for it.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.380
We're starting off with
some Thai red curry paste.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.680
Gonna add coconut milk,
water, soy sauce, fish sauce.

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.470
And then just like a little pinch of sugar

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.345
to balance out all those flavors.

00:04:14.345 --> 00:04:17.960
Then I've just julienned
some snow peas just to,

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.230
one, add your veggies and give
it a little bit of crunch.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.300
Then I've broken up some
rice noodles in half.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.860
I'm just gonna stick them in there.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:25.990
Now onto the shrimp.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.480
We are starting with frozen raw shrimp

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.840
and this is so it doesn't
over cook in the microwave.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.770
If you're a little worried
about microwaving shrimp,

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:35.300
just make sure that it
is opaque throughout

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.630
and not translucent.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.270
I forgot to add my aromatics,

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:43.340
so we are just gonna add a
little bit of ginger powder

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.750
and garlic powder.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:46.495
We know Jasmine loves garlic.

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:48.385
So I'm gonna cover it with a plate

00:04:48.385 --> 00:04:50.420
and then pop it in the microwave

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.584
for three and a half minutes.

00:04:51.584 --> 00:04:53.350
(microwave beeping)

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.770
All right.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.950
It smells so good.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.463
That's what's expected.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.950
Look at that!

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.853
My shrimp are cooked, the
vegetables stayed green.

00:05:04.853 --> 00:05:06.654
That's really surprising.

00:05:06.654 --> 00:05:08.418
The noodles look tender.

00:05:08.418 --> 00:05:09.818
If you take it out and your noodles

00:05:09.818 --> 00:05:11.253
are still a little bit crunchy,

00:05:11.253 --> 00:05:13.110
just pop it back in the microwave for like

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.000
another minute or two,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.500
'cause you really want them
to be al dente and not raw.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.340
To add a little pizazz,

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.080
we're just gonna garnish
it with fresh cilantro.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:22.260
I can't wait for her to try this.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:23.281
It smells so good.

00:05:23.281 --> 00:05:24.530
Let's see if she likes it.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.020
All right, here's your lunch.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.530
- [Jasmine] Thank you!
- You're welcome.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.140
- Oh my goodness.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.594
You know I love a good nood.

00:05:30.594 --> 00:05:32.402
(Kelly laughs)
Dle, dle.

00:05:32.402 --> 00:05:34.778
- I didn't know you love a good nood.

00:05:34.778 --> 00:05:36.280
- Dle.
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:37.661
Cheers!

00:05:37.661 --> 00:05:39.780
(Jasmine moans)

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.310
- Would you ever know
that was from a microwave?

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.650
- Mm-mm, never!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.310
Cooked through, al dente,
like it was like perfect.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:47.300
Big yay from me.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.463
- Two yays so far.

00:05:48.463 --> 00:05:50.290
Now I'm gonna make you dinner.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.203
- Thank you so much.

00:05:51.203 --> 00:05:52.153
(Kelly laughs)

00:05:52.153 --> 00:05:54.430
- I'm so excited about this one.

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.239
We're making risotto in the microwave.

00:05:56.239 --> 00:05:57.590
We're adding mushrooms,
we're adding thyme.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.612
It's gonna be so delicious.

00:05:59.612 --> 00:06:02.360
So we just got some butter and onions.

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.840
We are going to saute our onions

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:06.840
for just about 60 seconds in the microwave

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.670
to get the cooking process
started and soften them up.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.200
The butter is melted.

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.653
They look a little bit softened.

00:06:12.653 --> 00:06:13.550
(bowl clanging)

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.800
Exactly what we want.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:19.440
I'm gonna add some garlic,
our mushrooms, some thyme.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.390
You can use fresh or
dried, doesn't matter.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:24.830
Arborio rice, a little bit of white wine.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:26.136
Whoa. (laughs)

00:06:26.136 --> 00:06:28.170
Got a little excited about the white wine.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.940
Don't worry about the
alcohol, it's gonna cook off,

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:31.640
but you can just leave it
out if you don't want it.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.940
And then a little bit of chicken stock.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.120
You can also use veggie
broth, whatever you like.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.350
All right, so I'm gonna put
this in the microwave covered

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.800
for eight minutes
stirring every 90 seconds

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.850
